{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.EightfoldWay.MesonOctetTracelessSplit","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.EightfoldWay.MesonOctetTracelessSplit","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.EightfoldWay.MesonOctetTracelessSplit.meson_split_dims","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.EightfoldWay.MesonOctetTracelessSplit.meson_split_dims","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/EightfoldWay/MesonOctetTracelessSplit.lean#L104-L109","doc":"**`n² = (n² − 1) + 1`** — the octet/singlet dimension count at general `n` (`n = 3` gives\n`9 = 8 + 1`).  Stated *after* the splitting and derived from `1 ≤ n²`, to make explicit that the\narithmetic is a **consequence** of the decomposition and not a substitute for it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.EightfoldWay.MesonOctetTracelessSplit.traceless_scalar_disjoint","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.EightfoldWay.MesonOctetTracelessSplit.traceless_scalar_disjoint","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/EightfoldWay/MesonOctetTracelessSplit.lean#L92-L100","doc":"**The sum is direct.**  A matrix that is both traceless and scalar is `0`.  This is the\n`⊕` in `𝟖 ⊕ 𝟏`: the octet and the singlet share nothing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.EightfoldWay.MesonOctetTracelessSplit.scalar_coeff_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.EightfoldWay.MesonOctetTracelessSplit.scalar_coeff_unique","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/EightfoldWay/MesonOctetTracelessSplit.lean#L79-L90","doc":"**The scalar coefficient is forced.**  If `M` splits as a traceless matrix plus `c • 1`,\nthen `c` is necessarily `tr M / n`.  Together with `traceless_add_scalar` this makes the\ndecomposition *unique*, which is what `⊕` asserts. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.EightfoldWay.MesonOctetTracelessSplit.trace_tracelessPart","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.EightfoldWay.MesonOctetTracelessSplit.trace_tracelessPart","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/EightfoldWay/MesonOctetTracelessSplit.lean#L68-L77","doc":"**The first summand is genuinely traceless** — this is where `(n : K) ≠ 0` is needed.\nOver a field whose characteristic divides `n` the scalar matrices are themselves traceless and\nno such splitting exists; the hypothesis is the real content, not bookkeeping. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.EightfoldWay.MesonOctetTracelessSplit.traceless_add_scalar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.EightfoldWay.MesonOctetTracelessSplit.traceless_add_scalar","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/EightfoldWay/MesonOctetTracelessSplit.lean#L62-L66","doc":"**The splitting exists.**  Every endomorphism is traceless-part plus scalar-part. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.EightfoldWay.MesonOctetTracelessSplit.tracelessPart","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.EightfoldWay.MesonOctetTracelessSplit.tracelessPart","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/EightfoldWay/MesonOctetTracelessSplit.lean#L58-L60","doc":"The traceless part: `M` minus its scalar part. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.EightfoldWay.MesonOctetTracelessSplit.scalarCoeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.EightfoldWay.MesonOctetTracelessSplit.scalarCoeff","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/EightfoldWay/MesonOctetTracelessSplit.lean#L54-L56","doc":"The scalar coefficient extracted from a matrix: `tr M / n`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}